Abstract: This paper proposes homogeneous function parameter packs for C++29: a variable number of parameters of one declared type. They would replace fixed-arity overload families with one declaration while retaining ordinary parameter initialization, conversion ranking, and a compile-time count.
Abstract:
Abstract: We seek Evolution Working Group direction on further work toward named packs and, separately, on reclaiming deprecated comma-less C varargs for unnamed packs. Reclamation changes existing meanings.
