# Implementation experience # {#implementation}

P1219R2 links an experimental <a href="https://github.com/Bekenn/clang/tree/func-parm-packs">Clang branch</a>. [[P1219R2]] Its tests, however, use the earlier <code>template &lt;&gt;</code> primary-template syntax. [[P1219-CLANG-TESTS]]

<aside class=issue>
<p>Complete and document an implementation of this revision's syntax and count model.</p>
</aside>

# Wording # {#candidate-rules}

For the independently selectable named feature, append the following requirement to the additions to <a href="[STD]temp.variadic#2">[temp.variadic]/2</a> in [[#wording-variadic]]:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack shall have a <var class=grammar ignore>declarator-id</var>.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

Retain the existing comma-less grammar, unnamed-ellipsis disambiguation, and deprecation text. If EWG approves reclamation, omit the name requirement and apply [[#wording-reclamation]]. Both choices share the count, deduction, and identity rules.

## Signatures ## {#wording-signatures}

The template-argument component of <a href="[STD]defns.signature.spec">[defns.signature.spec]</a> and <a href="[STD]defns.signature.member.spec">[defns.signature.member.spec]</a> already covers the invented count. We therefore need neither a signature change nor a separate pack-length component.

## Lambdas ## {#wording-lambdas}

In <a href="[STD]expr.prim.lambda.general#6">[expr.prim.lambda.general]/6</a>, insert after the first sentence:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>A lambda is a generic lambda if the <var class=grammar ignore>lambda-expression</var> has any generic parameter type placeholders (<a href="[STD]dcl.spec.auto">[dcl.spec.auto]</a>), or if the lambda has a <var class=grammar ignore>template-parameter-list</var>.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A <var class=grammar ignore>lambda-expression</var> is also a generic lambda if its <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration-clause</var> declares a homogeneous function parameter pack (<a href="[STD]temp.variadic">[temp.variadic]</a>).</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

In <a href="[STD]expr.prim.lambda.general#6">[expr.prim.lambda.general]/6</a>, append to Example 4:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane diff-code">
