## Variadic templates ## {#wording-variadic}

In <a href="[STD]temp.variadic#2">[temp.variadic]/2</a>, insert after the first sentence:

<div class="wording-diff diff-single">
<div class="diff-pane">
<p class="diff-label">Context and addition</p>
<div class="diff-line diff-context"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true"> </span><p>A function parameter pack is a function parameter that accepts zero or more function arguments.</p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>For a <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration</var> that declares a function parameter pack, its <em>parameter pattern</em> is the <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration</var> with the ellipsis in its declarator or <var class=grammar ignore>abstract-declarator</var> removed. The unexpanded packs in the parameter pattern are determined after introducing any template parameter corresponding to a generic parameter type placeholder in the declaration (<a href="[STD]dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>).</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>If the parameter pattern contains no unexpanded packs, the declaration declares a <em>homogeneous function parameter pack</em>. Otherwise, it declares a function parameter pack that is a pack expansion whose pattern is the parameter pattern. This classification is determined before substituting template arguments from an enclosing templated entity and is not changed by that substitution.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack shall declare parameters of the function declared by a function declaration or of a lambda's function call operator template.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>A homogeneous function parameter pack has an associated invented constant template parameter, its <em>count parameter</em>. The type of the count parameter is the type of a <code>sizeof</code> expression (<a href="[STD]expr.sizeof">[expr.sizeof]</a>). The value of the count parameter is the <em>pack count</em> and specifies the number of function parameters introduced by the pack. A homogeneous function parameter pack shall be the last parameter of its <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration-clause</var>. That <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration-clause</var> shall have the form <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration-list</var>. No other parameter of that clause shall be a function parameter pack.</ins></p></div>
<div class="diff-line diff-insert"><span class="diff-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p><ins>The type of each parameter introduced by a homogeneous function parameter pack is obtained from its parameter pattern by substitution and the parameter type adjustments specified in <a href="[STD]dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>. Substitution into the type specified by the parameter pattern is performed even when the pack count is zero. Each parameter so introduced is considered to have been expanded from the homogeneous function parameter pack. The value of a <code>sizeof...</code> expression naming this pack is the pack count.</ins></p></div>
</div>
</div>

Replace <a href="[STD]temp.variadic#6.1">[temp.variadic]/6.1</a> with:

<blockquote class=wording-inline>
<p>In a function parameter pack <ins>that is a pack expansion </ins>(<a href="[STD]dcl.fct">[dcl.fct]</a>); the pattern is <del>the <var class=grammar ignore>parameter-declaration</var> without the ellipsis</del><ins>its parameter pattern</ins>.</p>
</blockquote>

Modify <a href="[STD]temp.variadic#8">[temp.variadic]/8</a> as follows:

<blockquote class=wording-inline>
<p><del>A pack whose</del><ins>An occurrence of a</ins> name <del>appears</del><ins>denoting a pack is unexpanded in a construct unless it is</ins> within the pattern of a pack expansion <del>is expanded by that pack expansion</del><ins>contained in that construct</ins>.<ins> A pack is unexpanded in a construct if the construct contains at least one such occurrence. An occurrence that declares a pack is not considered when determining unexpanded packs.</ins></p>
<p><del>An appearance of the name of</del><ins>Each occurrence of a name denoting</ins> a pack is only expanded by the innermost <del>enclosing </del>pack expansion<ins> whose pattern contains that occurrence</ins>. The pattern of a pack expansion shall <del>name</del><ins>contain</ins> one or more <del>packs that are not expanded by a nested pack expansion; such packs are called </del>unexpanded packs<del> in the pattern</del>.</p>
<p>All of the packs expanded by a pack expansion shall have the same number of arguments specified. An appearance of a name of a pack that is not expanded is ill-formed.</p>
</blockquote>

Retain the remaining requirements of paragraph 8, the other expansion patterns in paragraph 6, and the element interpretations in paragraph 9.

Replace the <code>all</code> example in <a href="[STD]temp.variadic">[temp.variadic]</a> with:

